{"id": "EUVD-2026-82218", "enisaUuid": "851253aa-9268-36ca-a2cc-efebbb15d628", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/core: Wait for RCU callbacks before unloading ib_core\n\nput_gid_ndev() is queued with call_rcu() and implemented in ib_core.\nStopping the workqueues does not drain callbacks already queued, so RCU\ncould invoke it after the module code has been unloaded.\n\nsynchronize_rcu() does not wait for callbacks. Wait for them after all\nproducers have stopped.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:11:19", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:05:43", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/82dfd1df456227279b1c8c648983a530f2612098", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1646e123e56c3ad679fbfb571e8eef6386efb729", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8e4f1677c09d75d738099f42afcf65d8587b664a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7853af5f15738dc00aebaa1fc9f1f0df40f6f603", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0d5817fa4819abdc445fa77b5be4f0d49334a864", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9d998297fdaf47492f6679287f6552879d1a7e3a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/48b72fa0d209a92fb51b834a6080171cfa207b2c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7d75592114d1664623c8cf191a12b38052c04483"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93110", "GHSA-7xfw-24xh-pg25"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "277e8494-fc9b-3e16-a4db-df7b9e012d3f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "943bd984b108b3bb778790c2da4ae8d186b547e6 <48b72fa0d209a92fb51b834a6080171cfa207b2c"}, {"id": "3ed13979-25c5-3db1-953d-e35230e0ec0b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "4c0f0f0b-29f6-386e-a9c9-bf7e7c6cd62d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "943bd984b108b3bb778790c2da4ae8d186b547e6 <1646e123e56c3ad679fbfb571e8eef6386efb729"}, {"id": "543fb41b-8999-328e-a283-15bb889bb47f", "product": {"name": "Linux",